  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">State Prison</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">State prison - Support to State Prison</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to construct a high security state-level prison with a capacity for 300 sentenced prisoners and 50 persons in pre-trial detention, according to the standards of the European Prison Rules and laws of BiH. Persons convicted by the State Court are presently held in outdated and overcrowded sub-standard Entity prisons in Foca and Zenica. These institutions are not suited to securely incarcerate and rehabilitate persons who have been convicted for crimes against humanity, genocide and organised crime. The risk of escape from the entity prisons is evident and damages the public&#x2019;s confidence in the Bosnian justice system. &#xa0;There are over 150 persons in the Entities&#x2019; prisons serving their sentences imposed by the verdicts of the State Court. The majority are persons sentenced by the verdicts of war crimes or organized crime. Many of the detainees are placed in the Entities&#x2019; detention units (prisons), sometime quite far away from the State Court (Banja Luka, Mostar, Prijedor). They need to be brought in and out for the trials by the court police on daily basis which impacts the financial and security aspects of the trials. 
&#xa0;
Non-existence of a state-level facility is therefore a problem in terms of security and cost-efficiency as well as impact on the budget of the Ministry of Justice of BiH. The objective of this project is to solve some of these issues by building a high security state-level prison in Sarajevo. BiH&apos;s reputation of being unable to deal with growing organised crime obviously also affects its international reputation, hampering international investments and tourism. A high security state prison would however help to rebuilding the public&#x2019;s confidence in the Bosnian justice system. The construction of a state prison also contains a rights dimension, since such a facility will introduce international human rights standards in the BiH prison system this would be a step towards European integration.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Syftet med projektet &#xe4;r att etablera ett satligt s&#xe4;kerhetsf&#xe4;ngelse    med kapactiet i enlighet med europeisk f&#xe4;ngelsestandard och national  lag. F&#xe4;nlelst kommer att inhysa 300 d&#xf6;mda f&#xe5;ngar och 50 h&#xe4;ktade d&#xf6;mda rspektive &#xe5;talade f&#xf6;r krigsf&#xf6;rbrytelser, korruption och organiserad   brottslighet. Den svenska finansieringen kanaliserars genom           Euuropar&#xe5;dets utveklingsbank (CEB).</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The aim of the project is to construct a prison and establish a high  security institution complianat with the standards of the European    Prison Rules and laws of BiH.  The prison will host 300 convicts and  50 detainees, sentenced and indicted for serious war crimes,          organised crime and corruption. Teh Swedish funds will be executed    through a co-financing through the CEB (Concil of Europe Dev Bank)</narrative>
  </description>
